# Holistic Growth Tracker — core rules

A peer-accountability platform for entrepreneur boards running the Wheel of Life
and Wheel of Business practice on a fortnightly review cycle. Full detail in
`docs/PROJECT_SPEC.md`; the agreed screens are in `docs/wireframe.html`.

## Invariants — never violate these

1. **Every score is self-rated.** Nothing is derived, averaged or rolled up.
   The business wheel never computes the Business spoke on the life wheel. If a
   feature would compute a score from other scores, stop and ask.

2. **Wheels, plans, tasks, notes and companies belong to the person, not the board.** Never add a
   `board_id` to `wheels`, `spokes`, `wheel_cycles`, `spoke_scores`,
   `focus_areas`, `action_plans`, `tasks`, `notes`, `note_files`, `note_categories`
   `note_comments` or `companies`. Members carry
   their history between boards, and that only works because the board does not own it.

3. **Everything below `wheels`, plus `notes`, is private to its owner.** No member,
   chairman or superadmin may read another person's wheels, scores, plans, tasks or
   notes. The only shared surface is: profiles of co-members, the board roster, the
   meeting calendar, the counts from `board_velocity`, and tasks the owner has
   ticked as shared with a board (through `board_shared_goals`, see 4).

4. **`board_velocity` and `board_shared_goals` are the only cross-member reads.**
   `board_velocity` returns counts and names only; never extend it to return
   titles, tags, dates or links. `board_shared_goals` returns task id, title,
   description, spoke names, start date, target date, status and progress (only for Work in Progress,
   Hold Now and Postponed) for tasks the
   owner shared with that board, and nothing else. Never extend it to notes,
   priority, tag, times or links, and never return an unshared task. Sharing is
   per task and per board, off by default, and only the owner can change it; it
   lives in `task_board_shares`, never as a `board_id` on `tasks`. Never add a
   third `SECURITY DEFINER` function that reads member content without asking.

5. **Never write `tasks.completed_on` from application code.** A database
   trigger owns it.

6. **Never delete a spoke.** Set `is_active = false`. A trigger blocks deletion
   once a spoke has history; surface its message rather than catching it.

## Deliberately absent — do not add without asking

Cross-member visibility beyond counts and explicitly shared tasks · sharing by
default · derived or averaged scores · notifications or nudges · definitions of what a score means · assigning tasks to
other people · completion-percentage metrics. (A progress number a member sets on one of
their own tasks is not that metric, and it must never be averaged, summed or
rolled up.)

Each of these was considered and rejected. The outcome this product is after is
a rounder wheel over time, not a productivity score.

## Tone of the interface

Sentence case. Plain verbs. No exclamation marks. A button says what happens and
keeps the same word through the flow. An empty screen invites an action; an
error says what happened and what to do next. Never apologise in UI copy.

## When unsure

`docs/PROJECT_SPEC.md` section 9 lists what was rejected and why. If a request
conflicts with an invariant above, say so rather than finding a way around it.
